  "details": "24265 `Download Prioritize Manually Shown`\n\nis the title of 2nd option of MM > Settings > Avatar > Avatar Download Prioritization\n\nThis `Manually Shown` means selecting the \"eye available icon\" option of \"Avatar Display\" on QM > User details > User Actions.  (see the 2nd image)\n\nI think this `Manually Shown` is unclear because:\n\n1. The QM does not express the selection as `Manually Shown` in a text but only in an icon.\n\n2. There are other options to show or hide avatars. These are the avatar options in the Safety Custom Shield Level and the avatar culling settings. So users could be confused or misunderstand it as meaning the other option.\n\nAnother string has the same issue: \n\n23179 `Allow override with \"Show Avatar\"`\n\nIIRC, the `Manually Shown` option in the QM (discussed above) was labeled \"Show Avatar\" in the old style QM. When written, 23179 may have been correct and precise, but it is not now. It becomes a misleading expression, especially for newcomers who don't see the old QM.\n\nSo, I offer reviewing and rewording these:\n\n- 23179 `Allow override with \"Show Avatar\"`   / option label in MM > Settings > Avatar > Avatar Culling\n\n- 14753 `Allow selected user's avatars to override culling settings.`  / tooltip of 23179\n\n- 24265 `Download Prioritize Manually Shown` / option label in MM > Settings > Avatar > Avatar Download Prioritization\n\n- 15167 `Click to prioritize downloading avatars from users you've manually shown.` / tooltip of 24265\n\n- 24903 `Shown avatar download prioritization disabled` / alert of 24265 becomes off\n\n- 24905 `Shown avatar download prioritization enabled` / alert of 24265 becomes on\n\n- 23185 `Prioritize Manually Shown Avatars` / outdated version of 24265? (See also Crowdin comment issue)",
